ut a vehicle and may include information from different sources. Public records may include: Ownership history Financial liens and administrative restrictions Roadworthiness inspections and technical checks Registration information Additional vehicle history information may include: Accident and damage records from multiple European countries, the US and Canada Estimated repair costs Mileage history and anomaly detection Stolen vehicle information Inspection history Import and export records And much more CARFAX offers tailored Vehicle History Reports for many European countries, including Italy, Spain, Poland, Germany and the Netherlands . Depending on the country, reports may contain market-specific information and can typically be accessed through the local language version of the CARFAX website. To check if a CARFAX Vehicle History Report is available, you will usually need either the vehicle's VIN (Vehicle Identification Number) or, in selected markets, the license plate. How long does it take to get a CARFAX report? The report is available instantly after payment . You will receive: A PDF version of your report by email immediately after purchase Access to the online version for 30 days What does this mean for you? You benefit from a broader view of the vehicle's history, including information that may exist outside the country where the vehicle is currently registered. You get immediate access to a vehicle history report, helping you understand the vehicle's background before making a purchase decision. Should there be any update on the data, reported to CARFAX on your specific car, the 30 days access will allow you to receive this update for free. After the 30 days period you will have to renew your access through purchase. More information. More context. More confidence."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where does CARFAX get its data?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The information in CARFAX Vehicle History Reports comes from a broad network of trusted sources across Europe and beyond. These sources may include: Government authorities and official vehicle registries Vehicle manufacturers Automotive associations Digital service and software providers Commercial data aggregators Workshops and dealerships Insurance-related sources where permitted Other businesses throughout the automotive value chain How we collect and use data We work exclusively with carefully selected and authorized partners. We do not use unauthorized data acquisition methods or scraping techniques. CARFAX combines publicly available information with data provided through long-term partnerships across the automotive industry and creates one of the most comprehensive vehicle history reports available in Europe. What does this mean for you? Instead of searching across multiple sources, you can review relevant vehicle history information in one place and make a more informed decision."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why do partners share their data with CARFAX?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Many of our sources deliberately choose CARFAX as their primary - and in some cases even exclusive - partner for sharing their data. That’s because this collaboration is not just about data sharing, but above all about bringing greater transparency to the used-car market. Partners trust CARFAX because we: Process data responsibly and carefully Use information in compliance with regulations Make vehicle reports quickly accessible and easy to understand"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why trust CARFAX?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For more than 40 years , CARFAX has helped consumers and businesses better understand vehicle histories. Today, CARFAX works with 100,000+ data sources and applies advanced report intelligence to transform complex data into clear, useful information. CARFAX strives to provide: Reliable information High-quality data Transparency for consumers What does this mean for you? When evaluating a used vehicle, you can rely on a report built from trusted sources and decades of vehicle history expertise."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What do customers appreciate about CARFAX reports?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Customers most frequently highlight the speed, clarity and depth of information provided by CARFAX. Fast Access Reports are available instantly Immediate online access after purchase Clear and Detailed Information Easy-to-understand report structure Detailed vehicle history information User-friendly presentation Comprehensive Coverage Extensive vehicle history data Cross-border information where available Multiple data sources combined in one report Reliability Information is perceived as trustworthy Customers frequently mention accuracy and consistency Peace of Mind Helps customers make better decisions Reduces uncertainty when buying a used vehicle Provides added confidence before purchase What does this mean for you? CARFAX helps simplify complex vehicle history information so you can make decisions with greater confidence."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What do less satisfied customers criticize?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some customers mention that a report contains less information than they expected. Typical concerns include: Limited available data for a specific vehicle Missing information they expected to find Reports that do not significantly affect their purchasing decision Why Does This Happen? The amount of available information depends on the individual vehicle. Information can vary depending on: The vehicle's history Whether events were recorded Data availability from source providers An Important Fact This is true for all vehicle history reports, not just CARFAX. No provider can guarantee a complete vehicle history or 100% coverage of all events. Some events may never have been recorded or shared through centralized systems. Our Approach We believe in transparency. That's why we: Share all available information Clearly explain limitations Continuously improve data coverage and quality What does this mean for you? You can evaluate a vehicle based on the information available while understanding any limitations in the underlying data."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is CARFAX worth the price?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A CARFAX Vehicle History Report can help you avoid costly mistakes when purchasing a used vehicle. The price of a report is typically small compared with the value of the vehicle and may help identify risks before you buy. What goes into a CARFAX Report? Creating a CARFAX report involves: Gathering data from 100,000+ sources Processing information from multiple countries Analyzing 45+ billion vehicle history records Cleaning and validating data Connecting records across systems and languages Delivering results instantly Trusted by Professionals CARFAX is used by: Thousands of dealers and business customers Leading automotive marketplaces Automotive professionals across Europe Millions of smart used car buyers worldwide Many dealers already use CARFAX and may provide a report as part of the buying process. What does this mean for you? You're not only accessing vehicle history information. You're using the same trusted standard relied upon by automotive professionals across Europe. And don't be shy to ask the seller for a CARFAX Report."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What can I do if I'm not satisfied with the CARFAX report?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can contact our Customer Support team at any time. Real people review your request Support is available when you need it Every enquiry is assessed individually If you're not satisfied with your purchase, CARFAX offers a 30-day money-back guarantee . What does this mean for you? You can purchase a CARFAX Vehicle History Report with confidence, knowing that support is available if you need assistance and that you're protected by our refund policy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does CARFAX have data that others don’t?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"CARFAX opera da anni nel mercato italiano e ha costruito nel tempo una rete solida di relazioni dirette con partner che lavorano quotidianamente sui veicoli. Questi partner - come officine e operatori del settore - vedono le auto nella pratica, non solo attraverso documenti amministrativi. Questo ci permette di raccogliere informazioni più concrete e vicine alla reale storia del veicolo. Il nostro approccio ai dati A differenza di altri operatori, CARFAX: segue rigorosamente le normative europee sulla protezione dei dati e dei consumatori si tiene lontana da pratiche illegali o poco trasparenti di acquisizione dei dati non utilizza scraping né fonti non autorizzate Investiamo invece in: partnership ufficiali e di lungo periodo gestione attiva e continuativa dei rapporti con i nostri partner standard elevati di qualità e affidabilità dei dati Perché i partner scelgono CARFAX Molte fonti scelgono CARFAX come canale principale — e in alcuni casi esclusivo — per condividere i loro dati. Questo avviene perché: sanno che trattiamo i dati con responsabilità e attenzione garantiamo un utilizzo conforme alle normative lavoriamo con l’obiettivo di creare più trasparenza nel mercato dell’auto usata Cosa significa per te CARFAX raccoglie dati da fonti selezionate e partner che lavorano direttamente sui veicoli, per offrirti una lettura più concreta della loro storia."}}]}]}</script><style>
